⚠️ **IMPORTANT: The new `ports` seam's ordering contract is untested — pin "first available port wins"**

The parameter's core semantic — *try the listed ports in order, bind the first one that succeeds* — has no test coverage after this change:

- `ports: const [0]` tests only cover a single-entry list (nothing to fall back from).
- «throws when both callback ports are occupied» pins the exhausted-list path only.

If someone reorders the default or breaks the `break` in the loop, every test stays green while the production contract (1455 preferred, 1457 fallback — the Codex-registered pair) silently changes. Cheap hermetic pin, no fixed ports needed:

```dart
test('binds the first available port and falls back to the next', () async {
  final occupant = await HttpServer.bind(InternetAddress.loopbackIPv4, 0);
  final server = ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer();
  // First port busy → second (also ephemeral) wins.
  final url = await server.start(
    timeout: const Duration(seconds: 5),
    ports: [occupant.port, 0],
  );
  expect(Uri.parse(url).port, isNot(occupant.port));
  await server.close();
  await occupant.close();
});
```

(Since both ports are registered with the provider, an order flip wouldn't even break sign-in immediately — which is exactly why only a test can catch it.)

⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Web stubs don't mirror the new `ports` parameter — the exact drift this repo documents as a web-only build break**

The IO implementations gained `List<int> ports = const [1455, 1457]`, but their web counterparts in `flutter_app/lib/services/oauth_cli_flow_stubs.dart` were not updated:

- `ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer.start({Duration timeout})` — no `ports`
- `runChatGptOAuthCliFlow({onStatus, openBrowserFn, exchangeFn, timeout})` — no `ports`

That stub file's own comment states the invariant this violates: *"The signature mirrors the IO implementation parameter-for-parameter (dart2js compiles the mobile branch even on web, so a missing named parameter is a web-only BUILD break the VM tests never see)."*

Nothing breaks today — verified no `flutter_app` caller passes `ports` — so this is latent debt, not a red build. But the first app-side caller that passes `ports:` compiles fine on macOS/VM and breaks the web build in a way the Dart VM test suite cannot see (per the file's own warning). Please mirror the parameter:

```dart
class ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer {
  /// Always throws on the web.
  Future<String> start({
    Duration timeout = const Duration(minutes: 5),
    List<int> ports = const [1455, 1457],
  }) => throw UnsupportedError('Local servers are not supported on the web.');
  ...
```

Related accuracy note: the PR description says provider_commands.dart:1288 is "the only prod caller" — `flutter_app/lib/services/chatgpt_oauth_flow.dart:187` (`runChatGptOAuthCliFlow`) and `:233` (`server.start()` in the iOS system-auth-session hop) also call this API. All use defaults, so the byte-identical-behavior claim still holds; the caller list in the description is just incomplete.

